      "writtenOn": "2022-09-20T16:47:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "http://go/cstyle#Structs_vs._Tuples \n\n\"Prefer to use a struct instead of a pair or a tuple whenever the elements can have meaningful names.\" \n\nConsider something like `private: struct StorageInfo { int count, reserve };`",
      "range": {
